From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the runtime pipeline report names a boot pipeline evicted before its first use as such, not "on disk, not built at boot" (log only, always on)

No switch: this changes log text only (see "Why unconditional").

Why: CreateGraphicsPipeline labels a pipeline made at run time "evicted" only when its key is in
used_and_evicted, and EvictUnusedPipelines puts a key there only when a draw had used the pipeline
this session. A pipeline the boot built and no draw had used yet, evicted at the first check after
9000 frames, fell through to "on disk, not built at boot", which says the opposite of what
happened. In the T151 play session of 13 Nov that was the bulk of the run-time builds: 2,278 boot
pipelines evicted at 204.9 s ("Evicted 2278 graphics pipelines unused for 9000 frames, 28 left"),
then 1,490 "on disk, not built at boot" from 227 s on, with EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES=1 (every
record that passes the boot's checks is built; no "built when first needed" line and no failed
boot build in that log, so these can only be evicted boot pipelines). It made the logs point at the
boot's preparation instead of at the eviction.

What: a new set evicted_unused (key hashes) gets the key of each pipeline EvictUnusedPipelines
destroys that was not in used_this_session; used_and_evicted (which feeds the used list the next
boot reads) is unchanged. The reason test is now: used_and_evicted -> "evicted"; evicted_unused ->
"built at boot, evicted before its first use" (new RuntimeBuild::EvictedUnused); disk_pipelines ->
"on disk, not built at boot"; else "new". The per-pipeline line shows the new text. The 10 s line
keeps its format "(new a, on disk b, evicted c, mesh d)" and counts the new reason under "evicted"
(it was built and evicted), so tools that read it keep working; comparisons with logs before this
patch must add earlier "on disk" counts to "evicted" for sessions with PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES.
A task/mesh pipeline is still reported as "mesh, not in the disk cache" unless EDEN_UP_MESH_CACHE=1
(unchanged). With EDEN_UP_BUILD_BURST_LOG=1 such a pipeline is classed Evicted, not Disk.

Why unconditional: no pipeline, cache file, used list or stamp changes; only the text of the
per-pipeline line and which column of the 10 s line counts these builds. Cost: one set insert per
pipeline evicted without a use (2,278 in that session), one more set lookup per run-time build.

T153 integration review: the insert into evicted_unused is wrapped in a std::bad_alloc catch.
This patch is always on and only labels, so a set that finds no memory now leaves the label out
(the line says "on disk" again) instead of throwing out of EvictUnusedPipelines on the GPU thread.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 6559efb..f5132dc 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -2708,6 +2708,13 @@ void PipelineCache::EvictUnusedPipelines() {
         }
         if (used_this_session.erase(pipeline) != 0) {
             used_and_evicted.insert(it->first.Hash());
+        } else {
+            // Built ahead (at boot) and never drawn: for the runtime report only. A label, so a
+            // set that finds no memory leaves it out ("on disk" again) instead of failing here.
+            try {
+                evicted_unused.insert(it->first.Hash());
+            } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+            }
         }
         if (EvictKeepSsbo()) {
             if (const auto* const slots = pipeline->MappedPointers()) {
@@ -3257,12 +3264,18 @@ namespace {
 // workers): every one over 2 ms is logged, and the total every 10 s, to tell how much of the
 // stutter on new content is translation. The reason and the key hash tell two runs' lists apart:
 // a pipeline with one hash in every run, not "new", is one the disk cache does not keep.
-enum class RuntimeBuild : size_t { New, OnDisk, Evicted, Mesh, Count };
+// EvictedUnused: a pipeline built ahead of its draws (at boot) and evicted before any draw used it
+// (EvictUnusedPipelines: its "last use" is the boot). Those were reported as "on disk, not built
+// at boot" (1,490 of 2,383 in the T151 play session of 13 Nov, after 2,278 boot pipelines were
+// evicted at 205 s); now each such line says so, and the 10 s line counts them as "evicted" (they
+// were built and evicted), so its format is unchanged.
+enum class RuntimeBuild : size_t { New, OnDisk, Evicted, Mesh, EvictedUnused, Count };
 
 void ReportRuntimePipeline(const char* kind, std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point begin,
                            RuntimeBuild reason, u64 hash) {
     static constexpr std::array<const char*, static_cast<size_t>(RuntimeBuild::Count)> names{
-        "new", "on disk, not built at boot", "evicted", "mesh, not in the disk cache"};
+        "new", "on disk, not built at boot", "evicted", "mesh, not in the disk cache",
+        "built at boot, evicted before its first use"};
     static std::array<u32, static_cast<size_t>(RuntimeBuild::Count)> reasons{};
     static std::chrono::steady_clock::duration total{};
     static u32 count{}, logged{};
@@ -3282,7 +3295,7 @@ void ReportRuntimePipeline(const char* kind, std::chrono::steady_clock::time_poi
         LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
                  "Runtime pipelines in the last 10 s: {} built, {:.1f} ms on the GPU thread "
                  "(new {}, on disk {}, evicted {}, mesh {})",
-                 count, ms(total), reasons[0], reasons[1], reasons[2], reasons[3]);
+                 count, ms(total), reasons[0], reasons[1], reasons[2] + reasons[4], reasons[3]);
         total = {};
         count = 0;
         reasons = {};
@@ -3359,9 +3372,10 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline() {
     Common::HangSite site{"building a graphics pipeline"};
     const auto begin = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     const u64 key_hash = graphics_key.Hash();
-    RuntimeBuild reason = used_and_evicted.contains(key_hash)  ? RuntimeBuild::Evicted
-                          : disk_pipelines.contains(key_hash) ? RuntimeBuild::OnDisk
-                                                              : RuntimeBuild::New;
+    RuntimeBuild reason = used_and_evicted.contains(key_hash)   ? RuntimeBuild::Evicted
+                          : evicted_unused.contains(key_hash) ? RuntimeBuild::EvictedUnused
+                          : disk_pipelines.contains(key_hash)  ? RuntimeBuild::OnDisk
+                                                               : RuntimeBuild::New;
     SCOPE_EXIT {
         ReportRuntimePipeline("Graphics", begin, reason, key_hash);
     };
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h
index 3eaea99..f8e121d 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h
@@ -281,6 +281,7 @@ private:
     u64 frame_count{};
     std::deque<std::pair<u64, std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline>>> evicted_pipelines; ///< (tick, pipeline)
     std::unordered_set<u64> used_and_evicted; ///< Key hashes of pipelines used this session, evicted since
+    std::unordered_set<u64> evicted_unused;   ///< ... and of those evicted before any draw used them
     /// EDEN_UP_EVICT_KEEP_SSBO: storage buffer pointer slots of evicted pipelines, by key hash
     VideoCommon::EvictedPointerSlots evicted_pointer_slots;
 
